FCNTL(2)                       P32W Unix                        FCNTL(2)

NAME
       fcntl - descriptor flags

SYNOPSIS
       #include <fcntl.h>

       int fcntl(int fd, int cmd, ... /* int arg */);

DESCRIPTION
       F_GETFL returns the descriptor's flags (O_RDONLY, O_WRONLY or
       O_RDWR, and O_APPEND, O_NONBLOCK); F_SETFL sets O_APPEND and
       O_NONBLOCK from arg, the others staying. With O_NONBLOCK a
       socket's calls fail with EAGAIN (connect: EINPROGRESS) rather
       than wait. F_DUPFD returns a copy of fd at the lowest free
       descriptor not below arg, as dup(2) does from 0. F_GETFD and
       F_SETFD are accepted (no close-on-exec yet: 0).

RETURN VALUE
       F_GETFL: the flags; F_DUPFD: the new descriptor; else 0. -1 on
       an error, with errno set.

ERRORS
       EBADF   fd is not open.
       EINVAL  An unknown cmd, or arg out of range for F_DUPFD.
       EMFILE  F_DUPFD: no descriptor free.

SEE ALSO
       open(2), dup(2), socket(2)

BUGS
       O_NONBLOCK affects sockets only: terminals and pipes still
       wait.
